WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
JENNY BROWN: Today,
we're talking

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:07.650
about I/O, 2022 summits, role
certifications, and a shift

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.590
in shopping habits that
might surprise you.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.980
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.810
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.870
Google I/O is back
May 11 through 12,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:25.190
and all content is virtual
and free for everyone.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.650
Connect with developers
from around the world

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:31.190
for thoughtful discussions,
learn from Google experts,

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:34.850
and get a first look at our
latest developer products.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.920
This year, the program looks
a little bit different.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.730
You can catch all keynotes,
product announcements,

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.520
and Learning Lab
content on day 1.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.270
And then come back for day 2,
when all technical sessions

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.520
will be available on demand.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.410
Register and check out
the program at io.google.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:58.580
Our 2022 Google Cloud Summit
Series is in full swing,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.700
and you can be among the first
to learn about new solutions

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.960
across data, machine learning,
collaboration, security,

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.490
sustainability, and more.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.420
We've got several events in
the upcoming weeks where you'll

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.780
hear from experts, explore
customer perspectives,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.510
engage with interactive
demos, and gain

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.660
valuable insights to help
you accelerate your business

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.010
transformation.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.530
Be sure to bookmark the
Google Cloud Summit Series

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.280
website to easily find
updates as news develops.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:31.430
We've rebranded the Professional
Collaboration Engineer

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.430
Certification to the
Professional Google Workspace

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.400
Administrator Certification,
and we've updated

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.260
the relevant learning path.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.050
Check out the blog for more
details and an interview

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.570
about the Google Workspace
administrator role

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.570
and how demand and
preparation for this skill set

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:49.610
has changed over the years.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:53.180
Shifting work habits, more
online shopping options,

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.260
rising inflation, and stretched
supply chains are just a few

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.230
of the factors making it
harder to discern what's

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.610
top of mind for shoppers today.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.060
And while price
unsurprisingly continues

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.850
to be a major
consideration in purchases,

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.070
the average shopper
is increasingly

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.760
paying close attention to the
values of consumer goods brands

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.570
and how eco-friendly their
products and practices are.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.300
Head to the blog to learn
more from this research

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.500
and how brands can adapt.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.870
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.670
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.310
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.680
Leave us a comment or tweet us,
and we'll see you in the Cloud.

